---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { THEMES, PROPHETS, DUAS, byTheme } from "../lib/content";
import quotes from "../../content/generated/quotes.json";

// Fetched and hash-locked like every other line of scripture on the site —
// never typed into this template. See scripts/fetch-quotes.ts.
const epigraph = quotes.find((q) => q.id === "call-upon-me")!;

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const prophetCount = PROPHETS.filter((p) => p.section === "prophet").length;
---

<Base
  title="The Duʿāʾ of the Prophets"
  description={`The supplications of the Prophets as recorded in the Qurʾān and the authenticated Sunnah — ${DUAS.length} duʿāʾ with Arabic, transliteration, translation, and the occasion each was said.`}
>
  <div class="stack" style="margin-top: var(--s-16); margin-bottom: var(--s-24)">
    <div>
      <h1 style="font-size: var(--t-2xl); max-width: 22ch">
        What the Prophets said, and what they were facing when they said it.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--s-6)">
        {DUAS.length} supplications from the Qurʾān and the authenticated
        Sunnah. Each one has its Arabic, how to say it, what it means, and the
        occasion it was said on.
      </p>
      {/*
        Descriptive, not doctrinal. An earlier draft asserted that "duʿāʾ is not
        a last resort" and that God "is the only one who gives or withholds".
        The first is an over-correction — Yūnus called from inside the fish, and
        that was a last resort. The second is a claim of belief stated in the
        site's own voice with no citation, which is the thing this project
        refuses to do anywhere else. So this paragraph now lists what the
        collection actually contains, every clause of it traceable to an entry
        on the site, and the āyah below says the rest.
      */}
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--s-4)">
        They were said in every kind of moment: before facing a ruler, over a
        marriage with no children, while fleeing, after a mistake that could not
        be undone, from inside the darkness — and in thanks once the thing asked
        for had come.
      </p>
      <p
        style="font-family: var(--font-util); font-size: var(--t-sm); color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: var(--s-3)"
      >
        <span
          lang="ar"
          dir="rtl"
          translate="no"
          style="font-family: var(--font-arabic); font-size: var(--t-md)">{epigraph.text}</span
        >
        <span> — “Call upon Me, and I will answer you.” Qurʾān {epigraph.ref}</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!--
      Two doors, and nothing else. "By need" comes first because someone
      arriving with a situation in mind does not yet know which prophet
      matched it.
    -->
    <nav aria-label="Ways in" class="stack">
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: var(--t-lg)">
          <a href={`${base}/themes/`}>I need words for…</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="lede" style="font-size: var(--t-base); margin-top: var(--s-2)">
          Forgiveness, a decision, provision, family, gratitude, illness, grief.
          Sixteen situations.
        </p>
        <ul class="themes" style="margin-top: var(--s-6)">
          {
            THEMES.map((t) => (
              <li>
                <a class="theme-link" href={`${base}/themes/${t.id}/`}>
                  <span class="theme-name">{t.label.en}</span>
                  <span class="theme-count">{byTheme(t.id).length} duʿāʾ</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size: var(--t-lg)">
          <a href={`${base}/prophets/`}>By prophet</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="lede" style="font-size: var(--t-base); margin-top: var(--s-2)">
          {prophetCount} prophets in the order they came, from Ādam to Muḥammad ﷺ —
          with the companion supplications kept separate.
        </p>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </div>
</Base>
